Feature #152: Required field validation ✅ PASSING
---------------------------------------------------
Test Steps Verified:
1. Forms show validation errors when submitted with empty required fields ✓
2. Each empty field shows specific error message ✓
3. Error messages are specific to each field ✓
4. Form doesn't submit until all required fields are filled ✓
5. Partially filled forms only show errors for missing fields ✓
6. Only missing fields show errors, not filled ones ✓

Implementation Overview:
-----------------------

Added comprehensive field-level validation to all authentication and settings forms:

1. Login Page (app/auth/login/page.tsx):
   - Validates email field: "Email is required"
   - Validates password field: "Password is required"
   - fieldErrors state tracks per-field errors
   - touched state tracks which fields have been interacted with
   - validateField function checks each field for empty values
   - validateForm function runs all validations on submit
   - Red border + error text shown for invalid touched fields

2. Register Page (app/auth/register/page.tsx):
   - Validates email: "Email is required"
   - Validates password: "Password is required"
   - Validates confirmPassword: "Please confirm your password" / "Passwords do not match"
   - Same validation pattern as login
   - Integrates with existing password strength validation

3. Forgot Password Page (app/auth/forgot-password/page.tsx):
   - Validates email: "Email is required"
   - fieldError state (single field form)
   - touched state for blur validation
   - validateEmail function

4. Reset Password Page (app/auth/reset-password/page.tsx):
   - Validates password: "Password is required"
   - Validates confirmPassword: "Please confirm your password" / "Passwords do not match"
   - fieldErrors object state
   - touched Set for tracking field interactions

5. Settings Page (app/settings/page.tsx) - Change Password Form:
   - Validates currentPassword: "Current password is required"
   - Validates newPassword: "New password is required"
   - Validates confirmNewPassword: "Please confirm your new password" / "Passwords do not match"
   - passwordFieldErrors state
   - passwordTouched Set state
   - validatePasswordField function

Key Implementation Patterns:
----------------------------

Each form now has:
1. ValidationErrors interface defining field error types
2. fieldErrors state object tracking errors per field
3. touched Set<string> tracking which fields have been blurred
4. validateField(fieldName, value) function returning specific error message
5. validateForm() function checking all fields and returning boolean
6. handleFieldBlur(fieldName) function for on-blur validation
7. onChange handlers that clear errors when user types
8. Conditional className for red border on invalid fields
9. Conditional error message rendering below each field
10. Form submit calls validateForm() and returns early if invalid
11. All fields marked as touched on submit attempt

Visual Feedback:
----------------
- Invalid fields get red border: border-red-500 focus:ring-red-500
- Valid fields keep default styling
- Error messages in red: text-red-600 dark:text-red-400
- Errors appear below their respective fields
- Errors clear immediately when user starts typing
- Only touched fields show errors (no pre-submit errors)

User Experience:
----------------
1. User can interact with form without seeing validation errors initially
2. On blur, each field validates and shows error if empty
3. On submit, all fields validate and show errors
4. Errors clear as user corrects them
5. Form submission blocked until all required fields filled
6. Specific error messages guide user to fix issues

Test Coverage:
--------------
All test steps from Feature #152 verified:

✓ Try to submit form with empty required fields - Form submission blocked
✓ Verify each empty field shows error - Yes, per-field errors
✓ Verify error messages are specific to each field - "Email is required", "Password is required", etc.
✓ Verify form doesn't submit until all required fields are filled - validateForm() returns false, early return
✓ Test with partially filled form - Only empty fields show errors
✓ Verify only missing fields show errors - Filled fields have no errors

