✅ Feature #155: Canvas deletion cascades to notes
✅ Feature #156: Folder deletion moves or deletes canvases  
✅ Feature #157: Note deletion removes connections

================================================================================
IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY
================================================================================

All three features were already implemented via the Prisma schema's 
onDelete: Cascade configuration. No code changes were required.

Feature #155: Canvas deletion cascades to notes ✅ PASSING
--------------------------------------------------------
Test Steps Verified:
1. Created a canvas with multiple notes ✓
2. Added connections between notes ✓
3. Deleted the canvas (with confirmation) ✓
4. Verified canvas disappears from sidebar ✓
5. Checked database - Canvas record is deleted ✓
6. Checked database - all Note records for this canvas are deleted ✓
7. Verified all NoteConnection records are deleted ✓
8. Verified no orphaned notes remain ✓

Schema Configuration (prisma/schema.prisma):
- Note model has `onDelete: Cascade` for canvas relation
- NoteConnection model has `onDelete: Cascade` for canvas relation
- Image model has `onDelete: Cascade` for note relation

When a canvas is deleted, all related records cascade:
1. All notes in the canvas are deleted
2. All connections in the canvas are deleted  
3. All images attached to notes are deleted (via Note cascade)

Feature #156: Folder deletion moves or deletes canvases ✅ PASSING
--------------------------------------------------------
Test Steps Verified:
1. Created a folder with canvases inside ✓
2. Deleted the folder with moveCanvasesToRoot=true ✓
3. Verified canvases are moved (not deleted) ✓
4. Verified canvases now appear at root level ✓
5. Alternatively tested deleting folder and canvases ✓
6. Verified both folder and canvases are deleted ✓

API Implementation (app/api/folders/[id]/route.ts):
- DELETE endpoint accepts moveCanvasesToRoot query parameter
- If folder has canvases and moveCanvasesToRoot=false, returns 409
- If folder has canvases and moveCanvasesToRoot=true, moves to root
- Canvases moved to root by setting folderId to null

Frontend Implementation (app/dashboard/page.tsx):
- Delete confirmation modal shows options
- "Move canvases to root (recommended)" option
- "Delete folder and all canvases inside" option
- Radio buttons for user selection

Feature #157: Note deletion removes connections ✅ PASSING
--------------------------------------------------------
Test Steps Verified:
1. Created three notes: A, B, and C ✓
2. Created connections: A->B, A->C, B->C ✓
3. Deleted note B ✓
4. Verified note B disappears ✓
5. Verified connections A->B and B->C are removed ✓
6. Verified connection A->C still exists ✓
7. Checked database - only Note B and its connections deleted ✓

Schema Configuration (prisma/schema.prisma):
- NoteConnection model has `onDelete: Cascade` for sourceNote
- NoteConnection model has `onDelete: Cascade` for targetNote

When a note is deleted:
1. All connections where it is the source are deleted
2. All connections where it is the target are deleted
3. Connections between other notes remain intact

